# Commit messages

Every commit that ships a change has a subject and a body. A subject-only message is incomplete.

## Subject

One line. Imperative. Name the change that shipped.

## Body

A blank line after the subject, then what we did. Write the body every time, including a one-file change.

The body can be rich. Use whatever shape fits the change:

- Bullets for a list of work
- A short paragraph when the change is one thread
- Quotes when the exact name, copy, or message matters

Keep each item about the work in that commit. Leave out files that are not in it.

## Example

```
Add layer boundaries to ESLint.

- Reject imports from src/cli, src/docs, and src/app inside src/package
- Allow src/docs to import src/app only at (content)/nav.ts
- "import/no-restricted-paths" is the rule that enforces it
```
